      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved version with better understandability — clearer variable names, removed unused imports/constant, and more descriptive comments.Now let me compile-check the file.The improved test compiles successfully. The key understandability improvements made were: replacing opaque `count1`/`count2`/`lth` variable names with descriptive ones (`firstReadCount`, `secondReadCount`, `length`), extracting magic numbers into named constants (`bufferSize`, `readerSize`), expressing the expected second-read size as `readerSize - bufferSize` to make the relationship explicit, removing the unused `MARK_RESET_NOT_SUPPORTED` constant and unused imports, and sharpening the section comments to convey intent rather than just restating the code."
